Rebuilds the contractual capture instrument (§4.4) from the scoped handoff:
the participant's only tool, filing every capture end-to-end with no manual
steps.

Backend (Netlify Functions + Netlify Database + Blobs):
- Migration 0010: capture_sessions, capture_components, append-only
  capture_verification_events, and a public-safe public_capture_log view.
- recording-session: context snapshot + session issue with a one-time,
  single-use, 10-minute challenge code, per-session upload token, and
  requirements read from the live record. Violation modes are gated on
  Amendment No. 5 being confirmed_signed with no open blocking conflict,
  read live from the governing-document registry.
- recording-attest: server-time compliance stamp, plus recording-started /
  take-incomplete / safety-stop transitions and private location check-in.
- recording-upload: chunked, resumable 5 MB-part uploads to Netlify Blobs;
  parts are never overwritten; completion triggers verification.
- recording-verify-background: hard gates (hash == attested, code window,
  duration) then Claude AI review of burned-in frames/stills; AI/API failure
  falls back to AP review, never a silent pass. Server-side publication
  routing by mode.
- capture-media: serves only verified public-scope media; private-ap
  captures (corrective sessions, meal photos, location) are structurally
  unreachable from any public URL.
- ap-capture-review: AP review surface and append-only overrides.

Client (/recording-assistant/, noindex, participant-only):
- app.js: <recording-assistant> session core, canvas overlay engine with the
  challenge code burned into every frame, all eight capture modes, and a
  safety stop that ends any take with no penalty and opens an AP review.
- upload-queue.js: IndexedDB-backed resumable upload queue that survives
  reloads and airplane mode, filing against the original attestation stamp.

PACKET_KEY is capture-only. Server time governs all deadlines. The signed
Amendment No. 5 PDF from the handoff is intentionally not committed, per the
repository's signed-PDF policy.

